---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { readFileSync, existsSync } from 'node:fs';

// Redesign task 19 (isintegrity, prototype lines 1504-1520). This is the REAL
// content-integrity page, describing the actual verify-gurbani system that
// gates this site's build (see verify-gurbani.mjs, wired into `npm run
// build` before `astro build`). Restyled to the ledger system; the numbers
// and the "How it works" methodology paragraphs below are the page's own
// pre-existing, verbatim copy -- only their container changed (client-JS
// `#stats` fetch/render -> a build-time read of the same
// public/data/verification.json file, same pattern web/src/lib/verification.ts
// already uses -- so the numbers render in raw HTML with JS disabled, per
// DESIGN.md Principle 3, instead of behind a "Loading..." placeholder).
//
// The three new sections the prototype adds -- "The gates" 3-up grid, the
// review-status chip legend + "Reviewed" paragraph, and the "What this is
// not" note -- do not exist on the live page today. They are added using the
// prototype's own copy, each grounded in a real, already-shipped fact
// elsewhere in this codebase rather than invented: gate 01 restates the same
// build-gating fact as the "Fail-closed matching" bullet below; gate 02
// ("Scholar board review") is the real review.astro workbench (course_drafts
// tracks reviewed_by/reviewed_at in schema.sql); gate 03 ("Source
// attribution") is the real author-as-professor sourcing already described
// on /open-data's Sources section (SikhLibrary). The "Reviewed" paragraph is
// grounded the same way (a named reviewer + reviewed_at date, from the same
// schema fields). "What this is not" reuses verify.astro's own already-
// shipped "not an accredited institution" sentence rather than drafting a
// new, unverified claim -- the prototype's "contested account" clause has no
// grounding anywhere in this codebase and was dropped, per Principle 4
// (trust is earned, not claimed).
let totals = { verified: 0, mismatch: 0, uncovered: 0 };
let coursesFullyVerified = 0;
let coursesWithQuotes = 0;
let snapshotAngs = 0;
try {
  if (existsSync('./public/data/verification.json')) {
    const d = JSON.parse(readFileSync('./public/data/verification.json', 'utf-8'));
    totals = d.totals || totals;
    coursesFullyVerified = d.coursesFullyVerified || 0;
    coursesWithQuotes = d.coursesWithQuotes || 0;
    snapshotAngs = d.snapshotAngs || 0;
  }
} catch { /* absent in dev -- page still renders */ }
const hasIssues = !!(totals.mismatch || totals.uncovered);
---
<Base title="Content integrity — Sikhi University" description="How we verify the Gurbani quoted across Sikhi University against the canonical text — the numbers, the method, and what's still in progress." ambient="study">
  <section class="wrap max-w-3xl py-14">
    <p class="eyebrow flex items-center gap-2.5 text-saffron-deep">
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-px w-6 bg-current opacity-50"></span>
      <span>Content integrity</span>
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-display-sm mt-3 text-navy">Every quoted <span class="gur" lang="pa">ਸ਼ਬਦ</span>, checked against the canonical text</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] font-sans text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">Accuracy is a release gate here, not a nicety. Each shabad embedded in a course is matched, at build time, against the canonical text of Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji. A quote that doesn't match — or cites the wrong ang — fails the build and cannot ship. These numbers are generated from that check, not written by hand.</p>

    <div class="mt-9 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-5 border-t-2 border-navy pt-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div>
        <div class="stat-mono"><span data-no-i18n>{totals.verified.toLocaleString()}</span><span>Quotes verified</span></div>
        <p class="mt-1 font-sans text-xs text-muted">matched to canonical SGGS</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="stat-mono"><span data-no-i18n>{coursesFullyVerified.toLocaleString()} / {coursesWithQuotes.toLocaleString()}</span><span>Courses fully verified</span></div>
        <p class="mt-1 font-sans text-xs text-muted">every quote checked, none failing</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="stat-mono"><span data-no-i18n>{snapshotAngs.toLocaleString()}</span><span>Angs in the snapshot</span></div>
        <p class="mt-1 font-sans text-xs text-muted">canonical reference pages</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {hasIssues && (
      <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-sm text-muted" data-no-i18n>
        {totals.mismatch ? `${totals.mismatch} quote(s) under review. ` : ''}
        {totals.uncovered ? `${totals.uncovered} quote(s) not yet in coverage (e.g. Dasam/Sarbloh).` : ''}
      </p>
    )}

    <h2 class="rule-navy mt-12 pb-2 text-xl font-bold text-navy" data-i18n="integrity.gates.h2">The gates</h2>
    <div class="mt-1 grid gap-x-9 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="border-t-2 border-navy pt-3.5">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-mono text-[11px] text-saffron-deep">01</span>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-[17.5px] font-bold tracking-tight text-navy" data-i18n="integrity.gate1.title">Gurbani verification</h4>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted" data-i18n="integrity.gate1.body">Every quoted line is checked against the canonical snapshot at build time. A mismatch fails the build — the course cannot publish.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-t-2 border-navy pt-3.5">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-mono text-[11px] text-saffron-deep">02</span>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-[17.5px] font-bold tracking-tight text-navy" data-i18n="integrity.gate2.title">Scholar board review</h4>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted" data-i18n="integrity.gate2.body">Doctrine, sources and citations are reviewed by named reviewers before publication, and again after substantive revision.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-t-2 border-navy pt-3.5">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-mono text-[11px] text-saffron-deep">03</span>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-[17.5px] font-bold tracking-tight text-navy" data-i18n="integrity.gate3.title">Source attribution</h4>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted" data-i18n="integrity.gate3.body">Courses are attributed to the scholar whose work they draw on, with the source text linked, not paraphrased away.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="rule-navy mt-12 pb-2 text-xl font-bold text-navy" data-i18n="integrity.status.h2">What the review status means</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
      <span class="chip-status border-ok text-ok" data-i18n="integrity.status.reviewed">REVIEWED</span>
      <span class="chip-status border-saffron-deep text-saffron-deep" data-i18n="integrity.status.inreview">IN REVIEW</span>
      <span class="chip-status border-muted text-muted" data-i18n="integrity.status.draft">DRAFT — NOT PUBLISHED</span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[74ch] font-sans text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-ink"><strong>Reviewed</strong> means a named member of the scholar board has read the course and signed off on its doctrine and sources on a stated date. It does not mean the board endorses every reading in it, and it does not make the course a consensus position of the Panth.</p>

    <div class="mt-9 max-w-[74ch] border border-line border-l-[3px] border-l-saffron-deep bg-surface px-5 py-4">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-saffron-deep" data-i18n="integrity.notthis.label">What this is not</p>
      <p class="mt-2.5 font-sans text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted" data-i18n="integrity.notthis.body">Sikhi University is not an accredited institution. Review here is scholarly, not regulatory — no external body validates these courses, no credit transfers, and a certificate from us is a record of completed coursework, nothing more.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="rule-navy pb-2 text-xl font-bold text-navy">How it works</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3.5 grid gap-2.5 text-muted">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Canonical source.</strong> The reference text is a committed snapshot of Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji from BaniDB. The check runs against that fixed snapshot, offline — never a live lookup — so the result is reproducible.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Fail-closed matching.</strong> Each quoted tuk is normalised (Unicode form, spacing, vishraam markers) and must appear in the canonical text of the ang it cites. Anything that doesn't positively match is not counted as verified.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Honest about coverage.</strong> This currently covers SGGS quotes. Quotes from Sri Dasam Granth and Sri Sarbloh Granth, and any ang not yet in the snapshot, are listed as <em>not yet verified</em> — never quietly counted as passed.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-muted">AI-drafted course prose is labelled "Created by AI" and is separate from this scripture check. Verification confirms the <em>quoted scripture</em> is faithful; it is not a scholarly endorsement of a course's interpretation.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-sm text-muted">The underlying data is open — see the catalogue metadata and this verification report as a downloadable, openly-licensed dataset on our <a class="underline" href="/open-data">open data page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
